{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.KnotFactorShellClosed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.KnotFactorShellClosed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorSpectralDerivation"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_shell_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_shell_closed","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.lean#L34-L62","doc":"**Corollary (shell-closed knot factor).**\n\nUnder the Markov equilibrium hypothesis on the trivial idempotent\n`e_{(n)}`, the knot factor equals one exactly. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:knot-factor-shell-closed","label":"cor:knot-factor-shell-closed","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.weight_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.weight_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.trivial_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.trivial_block","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.vanish_offblock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.vanish_offblock","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.trivial_in","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.trivial_in","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium.mk","kind":"ctor","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovEquilibrium","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-shell-closed.lean#L21-L32","doc":"**Markov equilibrium hypothesis.**  For shell-closed `Z = N`\neven-even nuclei, every `λ ≠ (n)` block of `β · β*` vanishes and\nthe trivial-block character ratio equals one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}